{"explanation":"Adds a versioned current-record representation while preserving the existing two-argument encrypt and one-argument decrypt entry points for legacy records. Current records explicitly initialize AES-GCM from a fresh nonce, retain the resulting encoded parameters, persist a wrapping-key identity, and expose package-private discriminator/identity accessors plus a dual-key decrypt path for coordinated callers to resolve current generated keys without changing legacy record decoding.","review_assumptions":["The encrypted-record serializer/deserializer retains private instance fields, as it already must for mCipherText, mParameters, mCipher, and mToken; it will therefore retain mRecordVersion and mWrappingKeyId for current records while absent fields deserialize as null for legacy records.","Coordinated Encryptor and MasterKey edits will call encrypt(SecretKey, SecretKey, String) only with their persistent generated current-key identity, and will use isCurrentRecord(), getWrappingKeyId(), and decrypt(SecretKey, SecretKey) to select the current generated key versus their legacy key.","AES/GCM/NoPadding on the supported Android versions accepts a 12-byte nonce and a 128-bit GCM authentication tag through GCMParameterSpec."],"no_change_required":false,"decision":"MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW","confidence":"medium","edits":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKey.java","original_code":"package org.fedorahosted.freeotp.encryptor;

import android.util.Log;

import java.io.IOException;
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;
import java.security.AlgorithmParameters;
import java.security.InvalidAlgorithmParameterException;
import java.security.InvalidKeyException;
import java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;

import javax.crypto.BadPaddingException;
import javax.crypto.Cipher;
import javax.crypto.IllegalBlockSizeException;
import javax.crypto.NoSuchPaddingException;
import javax.crypto.SecretKey;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;

public final class EncryptedKey {
    private final byte[] mCipherText;
    private final byte[] mParameters;
    private final String mCipher;
    private final String mToken;

    private EncryptedKey(Cipher cipher, SecretKey token)
            throws BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException {
        mCipher = cipher.getAlgorithm();
        mToken = token.getAlgorithm();

        cipher.updateAAD(mToken.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        mCipherText = cipher.doFinal(token.getEncoded());
        mParameters = cipher.getParameters().getEncoded();
    }

    public static EncryptedKey encrypt(SecretKey key, SecretKey plaintext)
            throws NoSuchAlgorithmException, NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeyException,
            BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException {
        if (key == null) {
            throw new InvalidKeyException("Key is null");
        }
        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding");
        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key);
        return new EncryptedKey(cipher, plaintext);
    }

    public SecretKey decrypt(SecretKey key)
            throws NoSuchPaddingException, NoSuchAlgorithmException, BadPaddingException,
            IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException, InvalidAlgorithmParameterException,
            InvalidKeyException {
        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(mCipher);
        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key);
        String algorithm = cipher.getParameters().getAlgorithm();

        AlgorithmParameters ap = AlgorithmParameters.getInstance(algorithm);
        ap.init(mParameters);

        cipher.init(Cipher.DECRYPT_MODE, key, ap);
        cipher.updateAAD(mToken.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        return new SecretKeySpec(cipher.doFinal(mCipherText), mToken);
    }
}
","edit_kind":"declaration","corrected_code":"package org.fedorahosted.freeotp.encryptor;

import android.util.Log;

import java.io.IOException;
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;
import java.security.AlgorithmParameters;
import java.security.InvalidAlgorithmParameterException;
import java.security.InvalidKeyException;
import java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;
import java.security.SecureRandom;

import javax.crypto.BadPaddingException;
import javax.crypto.Cipher;
import javax.crypto.IllegalBlockSizeException;
import javax.crypto.NoSuchPaddingException;
import javax.crypto.SecretKey;
import javax.crypto.spec.GCMParameterSpec;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;

public final class EncryptedKey {
    private static final int CURRENT_RECORD_VERSION = 1;
    private static final int GCM_NONCE_LENGTH_BYTES = 12;
    private static final int GCM_TAG_LENGTH_BITS = 128;
    private static final SecureRandom SECURE_RANDOM = new SecureRandom();

    private final byte[] mCipherText;
    private final byte[] mParameters;
    private final String mCipher;
    private final String mToken;
    private final Integer mRecordVersion;
    private final String mWrappingKeyId;

    private EncryptedKey(Cipher cipher, SecretKey token, Integer recordVersion,
            String wrappingKeyId)
            throws BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException {
        mCipher = cipher.getAlgorithm();
        mToken = token.getAlgorithm();
        mRecordVersion = recordVersion;
        mWrappingKeyId = wrappingKeyId;

        cipher.updateAAD(mToken.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        mCipherText = cipher.doFinal(token.getEncoded());
        mParameters = cipher.getParameters().getEncoded();
    }

    public static EncryptedKey encrypt(SecretKey key, SecretKey plaintext)
            throws NoSuchAlgorithmException, NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeyException,
            BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException {
        if (key == null) {
            throw new InvalidKeyException("Key is null");
        }
        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding");
        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key);
        return new EncryptedKey(cipher, plaintext, null, null);
    }

    public static EncryptedKey encrypt(SecretKey key, SecretKey plaintext, String wrappingKeyId)
            throws NoSuchAlgorithmException, NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeyException,
            BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException {
        if (key == null) {
            throw new InvalidKeyException("Key is null");
        }
        if (wrappingKeyId == null || wrappingKeyId.isEmpty()) {
            throw new InvalidKeyException("Current wrapping key identity is missing");
        }

        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding");
        byte[] nonce = new byte[GCM_NONCE_LENGTH_BYTES];
        SECURE_RANDOM.nextBytes(nonce);
        try {
            cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key,
                    new GCMParameterSpec(GCM_TAG_LENGTH_BITS, nonce));
        } catch (InvalidAlgorithmParameterException e) {
            InvalidKeyException invalidKey = new InvalidKeyException(
                    "Unable to initialize AES-GCM parameters");
            invalidKey.initCause(e);
            throw invalidKey;
        }
        return new EncryptedKey(cipher, plaintext, CURRENT_RECORD_VERSION, wrappingKeyId);
    }

    boolean isCurrentRecord() {
        return Integer.valueOf(CURRENT_RECORD_VERSION).equals(mRecordVersion);
    }

    String getWrappingKeyId() {
        return isCurrentRecord() ? mWrappingKeyId : null;
    }

    public SecretKey decrypt(SecretKey key)
            throws NoSuchPaddingException, NoSuchAlgorithmException, BadPaddingException,
            IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException, InvalidAlgorithmParameterException,
            InvalidKeyException {
        return decrypt(key, key);
    }

    SecretKey decrypt(SecretKey legacyKey, SecretKey currentKey)
            throws NoSuchPaddingException, NoSuchAlgorithmException, BadPaddingException,
            IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException, InvalidAlgorithmParameterException,
            InvalidKeyException {
        SecretKey key;
        if (mRecordVersion == null) {
            key = legacyKey;
        } else if (isCurrentRecord()) {
            if (mWrappingKeyId == null || mWrappingKeyId.isEmpty()) {
                throw new InvalidKeyException("Current record is missing its wrapping key identity");
            }
            key = currentKey;
        } else {
            throw new InvalidKeyException("Unsupported encrypted key record version");
        }

        if (key == null) {
            throw new InvalidKeyException("Key is null");
        }

        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(mCipher);
        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key);
        String algorithm = cipher.getParameters().getAlgorithm();

        AlgorithmParameters ap = AlgorithmParameters.getInstance(algorithm);
        ap.init(mParameters);

        cipher.init(Cipher.DECRYPT_MODE, key, ap);
        cipher.updateAAD(mToken.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        return new SecretKeySpec(cipher.doFinal(mCipherText), mToken);
    }
}
","reason":"Preserves legacy records with no discriminator and their existing stored-parameter/AAD decryption path. Adds an explicitly initialized current AES-GCM record format with a fresh nonce, version discriminator, and wrapping-key identity; coordinated same-package callers can inspect the identity and provide separate legacy/current keys so decryption selects the correct path." ,"symbol":"EncryptedKey.encrypt and the corresponding encrypted-record decryption/serialization paths"}],"manual_review_required":true,"provided_contracts":["Existing public EncryptedKey.encrypt(SecretKey, SecretKey) continues to produce and decrypt the legacy representation.","Current writes must call public EncryptedKey.encrypt(SecretKey wrappingKey, SecretKey plaintext, String wrappingKeyId); wrappingKeyId must be non-null and non-empty.","Same-package callers select a decrypt key by calling isCurrentRecord() and getWrappingKeyId(), then call decrypt(SecretKey legacyKey, SecretKey currentKey); records lacking mRecordVersion select legacyKey, while version 1 records select currentKey.","Current record version is 1 and current records serialize mWrappingKeyId along with the existing cipher transformation, token algorithm, ciphertext, and encoded Cipher parameters."],"required_contracts":["Encryptor and MasterKey must resolve the generated current wrapping key using getWrappingKeyId() for current records and must continue supplying their existing legacy key as the first decrypt argument for records without a discriminator.","Encryptor and MasterKey must route all new current writes through encrypt(SecretKey, SecretKey, String) with the persistent generated-key identity.","The dedicated instrumentation test must construct/read legacy records through the retained two-argument encrypt/decrypt entry points and test current records through the three-argument encrypt and dual-key decrypt paths."],"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKey.java","required_tests":["Verify a legacy-format record created through encrypt(SecretKey, SecretKey) decrypts through decrypt(legacyKey, currentKey) using legacyKey.","Verify a current-format record created through encrypt(SecretKey, SecretKey, String) decrypts through decrypt(legacyKey, currentKey) using currentKey and exposes its supplied wrapping-key identity.","Encrypt two current records under one key identity, assert their retained encoded Cipher parameters differ, and verify both decrypt.","Verify current records reject a missing wrapping-key identity and unsupported non-null record versions fail rather than falling back to the legacy key."]}
